load 0
=== options
--- kate -
--author 	show the authors
--desktopfile=	the base name of the program's desktop entry
--display=	the X display, instead of $DISPLAY
--dograb 	grab the mouse, even in a debugger
--geometry=	geometry of the main window (100x100+50+50)
--help-all 	show the help, with Qt's options
--icon=	default window icon
--license 	show the license
--name=	instance name (ICCCM 4.1.2.5)
--nograb 	never grab the mouse
--platform=	the QPA plugin (NAME[:OPTIONS])
--platformpluginpath=	path to the platform plugins
--platformtheme=	platform theme
--plugin=	additional plugin to load
--qmljsdebugger=	activate the QML/JS debugger (port:1234[,block])
--qwindowgeometry=	geometry of the main window (100x100+50+50)
--qwindowicon=	default window icon
--qwindowtitle=	title of the first window
--reverse 	lay out right to left
--session=	restore the program from an earlier session
--startanon 	start with a new anonymous session (implies -n)
--tempfile 	delete the files after use
--title=	title of the first window
--visual=	ID of the X11 visual to use
-b 	wait for the running kate to close the files
-c 	go to this column
-e 	the encoding of the files to open
-h 	show the help
-i 	read the contents of standard input
-l 	go to this line
-n 	start a new kate, even if one is running
-p 	reuse only the kate with this pid
-s 	start with a session
-v 	show the version
--- kate --s
--session=	restore the program from an earlier session
--start=	start with a session
--startanon 	start with a new anonymous session (implies -n)
--stdin 	read the contents of standard input
--- kate -n
-n 	start a new kate, even if one is running
